WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.737
Pretraining, fine-tuning, and inference describe three different stages.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:11.477
Pretraining learns broad language patterns from a very large corpus using a general objective.

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:16.402
It is computationally expensive and produces the starting checkpoint.

00:00:16.402 --> 00:00:22.642
Fine-tuning continues training from that checkpoint on a smaller task or domain dataset.

00:00:22.642 --> 00:00:29.887
For example, a pretrained encoder can be fine-tuned to classify support tickets into categories.

00:00:29.887 --> 00:00:37.077
During fine-tuning, at least some model parameters are updated based on task-specific loss.

00:00:37.077 --> 00:00:43.347
Inference happens after training. We pass new text to the model and obtain predictions, embeddings,

00:00:43.347 --> 00:00:48.022
or generated text without updating the weights.

00:00:48.022 --> 00:00:53.597
Prompting belongs to inference: changing the instructions changes the input, not the parameters.

00:00:53.597 --> 00:00:59.857
Keeping these terms separate helps when reading model cards and papers.

00:00:59.857 --> 00:01:06.067
Ask: what was learned during pretraining, what additional adaptation happened afterward,

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.540
and what are we doing now at inference time?
